
# Riot API key handoff file (never commit a key)
riot-key.txt
frontend/riot-key.txt

# Local secrets for the end-to-end tests (test account credentials).
# The password manager is the source of truth; this is only a convenience copy.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Firebase CLI debug output
firebase-debug.log
api/firebase-debug.log
*.log

# A timeline document made locally by scripts/dev-timeline.mjs (10 Sep 2026): it lands in the
# working directory by default and carries our players' names, so it never goes in.
dev-timeline-*.json

# What scripts/replay-recorder.mjs leaves on disk (10 Sep 2026): the frames the League
# client renders while it walks a replay, and the documents a --dry-run writes instead of
# uploading. Pictures of our own game, several megabytes a run, and already in Firestore
# once the run finishes — none of it belongs in the repo.
replay-shots/
replay-recording-*.json
replay-shot-*.json

# The root package gained its first dependency on 11 Sep 2026 (`sharp`, for the recorder's
# frames), and with it a node_modules of its own. `frontend/` and `api/` each ignored theirs;
# the root never had to, so an `npm install` here left several thousand untracked files in
# front of the next `git add .`.
/node_modules/

# Stamped at build time by scripts/gen-build-info.mjs so the deployed site can say
# which commit it is (12 Sep 2026). Unlike build-info.ts nothing imports it, so it
# does not need a committed placeholder — the prebuild always writes it.
frontend/public/build.json
